    {
      "id": "77068cbebed6-q2",
      "number": 2,
      "question": "A field is in the shape of a rhombus, whose perimeter is 292 m and one of its diagonals is 96 m. What is the area of the field?",
      "questionHtml": "A field is in the shape of a rhombus, whose perimeter is 292 m and one of its diagonals is 96 m. What is the area of the field?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "4800 m 2",
          "html": "4800 m<sup>2</sup>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "7008 m 2",
          "html": "7008 m<sup>2</sup>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "5280 m 2",
          "html": "5280 m<sup>2</sup>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "5040 m 2",
          "html": "5040 m<sup>2</sup>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p style=\"\">4 × side = 292 cm ⇒ side = 73 cm</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">Let the other diagonal be D.</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"\">Side</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span><span style=\"\"> = </span><span class=\"math-tex\">\\({({Longer\\ diagonal \\over 2})^2 +({Shorter\\ diagonal \\over 2})^2 }\\)</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">73<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span> = (96/2)<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span> + (D/2)<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span>⇒ (D/2)<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span> = 73<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span> - 48<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2 </span> = 55<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span> ⇒ D/2 = 55 ⇒ D = 110</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">Hence, the area of the rhombus field = <span style=\"\"> Product of the lengths of two diagonals ÷ 2 =</span> <span class=\"math-tex\">\\({110 × 96} \\over 2\\)</span> = 5280 cm<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span></p>\n",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "77068cbebed6-q3",
      "number": 3,
      "question": "If one diagonal of a rhombus is equal to its side, then the diagonals of the rhombus are in the ratio of:",
      "questionHtml": "If one diagonal of a rhombus is equal to its side, then the diagonals of the rhombus are in the ratio of:",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "&radic;3 ∶ &radic;6",
          "html": "&radic;3&nbsp;∶&nbsp;&radic;6"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "&radic;2 ∶ 1",
          "html": "&radic;2&nbsp;∶&nbsp;1"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "&radic;2 ∶ &radic;3",
          "html": "&radic;2&nbsp;∶&nbsp;&radic;3"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "1 ∶ &radic;3",
          "html": "1 ∶ &radic;3"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/24/02/F2_SSC_Priya_13-2-24_D18.png\" style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); width: 306px; height: 192px;\" /></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">In △DOC ⇒ CD<span style=\"position: relative;  line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span> = OC<span style=\"position: relative;  line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span> + OD<span style=\"position: relative;  line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span> ⇒ A<span style=\"position: relative;  line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span> = (A/2)<span style=\"position: relative;  line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span> + OD<span style=\"position: relative;  line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span> ⇒ OD<span style=\"position: relative;  line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span> = A<span style=\"position: relative;  line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span> - (A<span style=\"position: relative;  line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span>/4) ⇒ OD = √3A/2. BD = OD + OB ⇒ 2 × √3A/2 ⇒ √3A</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Required Ratio = AC : BD ⇒ A : √3A = 1 : √3</p>\n",
      "images": [
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/24/02/F2_SSC_Priya_13-2-24_D18.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
