    {
      "id": "77068cbebed6-q4",
      "number": 4,
      "question": "The area of a rhombus is 2520 cm 2 and one of its diagonals is 90 cm. What is the perimeter of rhombus?",
      "questionHtml": "The area of a rhombus is 2520 cm<span style=\"position: relative;  line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span>&nbsp;and one of its diagonals is 90 cm. What is the perimeter of rhombus?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "210 cm",
          "html": "210 cm"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "220 cm",
          "html": "220 cm"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "216 cm",
          "html": "216 cm"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "212 cm",
          "html": "212 cm"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Given :</strong></p>\n\n<p>Area of Rhombus = 2520 cm<sup>2</sup></p>\n\n<p>One of it&#39;s Diagonal = 90 cm</p>\n\n<p><strong>Formula Used :&nbsp;</strong></p>\n\n<p>Area of Rhombus = 1/2&nbsp;&times; d<strong><sub>1</sub></strong>&nbsp;&times; d<sub>2</sub></p>\n\n<p>Perimeter = 4&nbsp;&times; Side</p>\n\n<p><strong>Calculation :&nbsp;</strong><br />\n<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/23/10/F2_Vinanti_Engineering_03.10.23_D5.png\" style=\"width: 132px; height: 146px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;2520 = 1/2&nbsp;&times; 90&nbsp;&times; d<sub>2</sub></p>\n\n<p>&rArr; d<sub>2</sub>&nbsp;= 5040/90 = 56</p>\n\n<p>Now,</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; d<sub>1</sub>/2 = 45 cm, d<sub>2</sub>/2 = 28 cm</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; AD&nbsp;=&nbsp;&radic;28<sup>2</sup>&nbsp;+ 45<sup>2</sup></p>\n\n<p>&rArr; AD =&nbsp;&radic;2025 + 784</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; AD =&nbsp;&radic;2809 = 53</p>\n\n<p>Perimeter = 4&nbsp;&times; 53 = 212 cm</p>\n\n<p><strong>&there4; The correct answer is 212 cm.</strong></p>\n",
      "images": [
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/23/10/F2_Vinanti_Engineering_03.10.23_D5.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "77068cbebed6-q5",
      "number": 5,
      "question": "In a rhombus ABCD, if &ang;ACB = 40&ordm;, then &ang;ADB = ?",
      "questionHtml": "In a rhombus ABCD, if &ang;ACB = 40&ordm;, then &ang;ADB = ?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "45&ordm;",
          "html": "45&ordm;"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "70&ordm;",
          "html": "70&ordm;"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "60&ordm;",
          "html": "60&ordm;"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "50&ordm;",
          "html": "50&ordm;"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<span style='display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;'><img height='26px' src='//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/shortcut-trick-image.png' width='26px' /> <u style='font-size: 21px; font-weight: 700; display: inline !important;'>Shortcut Trick</u></span>\n\n<p>In a <strong>rhombus</strong>, the <strong>diagonals</strong> are perpendicular to each other, so the angle at the intersection point is 90º (∠AOD = 90º).</p>\n<p>Since opposite sides of a rhombus are parallel (AD || BC), the <strong>alternate interior angles</strong> are equal:</p>\n<p>⇒ ∠DAC = ∠ACB = 40º</p>\n<p>In the right-angled triangle AOD, the sum of acute angles is 90º:</p>\n<p>⇒ ∠ADB = 90º − ∠DAC = 90º − 40º = 50º.</p>\n<p><strong>∴ The correct answer is 50º.</strong></p>\n\n<p><span style='display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;'><img height='26px' src='//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/alternate-methord-image.png' width='26px' /><strong><span style='vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;'><u>Alternate Method</u></span></strong></span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Given:</strong></p>\n<p>In a <strong>rhombus ABCD</strong>, the angle ∠ACB = 40º.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Properties Used:</strong></p>\n<p>1. The <strong>diagonals of a rhombus</strong> bisect each other at <strong>right angles</strong> (90º).</p>\n<p>2. Opposite sides of a rhombus are <strong>parallel</strong> (AD || BC).</p>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: left;\"><img src=\"https://cdn.testbook.com/tb_solImg_7e5ee0cc.png/1784541851.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto;\"></div>\n\n<p><strong>Calculations:</strong></p>\n<p>Let the diagonals AC and BD intersect each other at point O.</p>\n<p>⇒ ∠AOD = 90º (Diagonals are perpendicular)</p>\n<p>Since AD || BC and AC is a transversal line:</p>\n<p>⇒ ∠DAC = ∠ACB (Alternate interior angles)</p>\n<p>Given that ∠ACB = 40º:</p>\n<p>⇒ ∠DAC = 40º</p>\n<p>Now, in <strong>triangle AOD</strong>, the sum of all interior angles is 180º:</p>\n<p>⇒ ∠ADB + ∠DAC + ∠AOD = 180º</p>\n<p>⇒ ∠ADB + 40º + 90º = 180º</p>\n<p>⇒ ∠ADB + 130º = 180º</p>\n<p>⇒ ∠ADB = 180º − 130º</p>\n<p>⇒ ∠ADB = 50º</p>\n<p><strong>∴ The correct answer is 50º.</strong></p>\n\n<p><span style='display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;'><img height='26px' src='//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png' width='26px' /><strong><span style='vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;'><u>Additional Information</u></span></strong></span></p>\n\n<p style='margin:8px 0 2px 0;font-weight:700;color:#222222;'>Properties of Rhombus Diagonals</p>\n<p style='margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#444444;'>The diagonals of a rhombus bisect each other at right angles (90º) and also bisect the internal angles of the vertices they connect.</p>\n\n<p style='margin:8px 0 2px 0;font-weight:700;color:#222222;'>Area of a Rhombus</p>\n<p style='margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#444444;'>The area of a rhombus can be calculated using the lengths of its diagonals: Area = (1 ÷ 2) × d<sub>1</sub> × d<sub>2</sub>, where d<sub>1</sub> and d<sub>2</sub> are the diagonals.</p>\n\n<p style='margin:8px 0 2px 0;font-weight:700;color:#222222;'>Relation between Sides and Diagonals</p>\n<p style='margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#444444;'>The sum of the squares of the diagonals is equal to four times the square of any side: d<sub>1</sub><sup>2</sup> + d<sub>2</sub><sup>2</sup> = 4 × a<sup>2</sup>, where a is the side length.</p>",
      "images": [
        "//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/shortcut-trick-image.png",
        "//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/alternate-methord-image.png",
        "https://cdn.testbook.com/tb_solImg_7e5ee0cc.png/1784541851.png",
        "//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "77068cbebed6-q6",
