      "question": "BD is a diagonal of a rhombus ABCD. If &ang;ADB = 50&deg;, then the measure of &ang; DCB is",
      "questionHtml": "<p>BD is a diagonal of a rhombus ABCD. If&nbsp;&ang;ADB = 50&deg;, then the measure of&nbsp;<span style=\"\">&ang;</span>DCB is</p>\n",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "60&deg;",
          "html": "60&deg;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "75&deg;",
          "html": "75&deg;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "80&deg;",
          "html": "80&deg;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "100&deg;",
          "html": "100&deg;&nbsp;"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/05/F5_Madhuri_Teaching_02.05.2022_D3.png\" style=\"height: 206px; width: 203px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>ABCD is a rhombus.</p>\n\n<p>All sides are equal for a rhombus<span style=\"\"> </span><span style=\"\">⇒ </span> AB = BC = CD = DA</p>\n\n<p>For △ABD, AB = DA  ∴ ∠ADB = ∠ABD = 5<span style=\"\">0°</span></p>\n\n<p>Now, ∠BAD = <span style=\"\">180º - (50° + 50°) = 8</span><span style=\"\">0°, For ABCD rhombus, ∠BAD = ∠DCB</span></p>\n\n<p>Hence,  <span style=\"\">∠DCB = 8</span><span style=\"\">0°</span></p>\n",
      "images": [
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/05/F5_Madhuri_Teaching_02.05.2022_D3.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
