    {
      "id": "77068cbebed6-q9",
      "number": 9,
      "question": "In the given figure, ABCD is a rhombus in which &ang;OCB = 60&deg; . Then, find the value of AC : BD.",
      "questionHtml": "<p>In the given figure, ABCD is a rhombus in which&nbsp;&ang;OCB = 60&deg; . Then, find the value of AC : BD.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/23/01/F1_Vinanti_SSC_02.01.23_D1_V3.png\" style=\"width: 194px; height: 131px;\" /></p>\n",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "&radic;3 : 4",
          "html": "&radic;3 : 4&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "4 : &radic;3",
          "html": "4 :&nbsp;&radic;3&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "&radic;3 : 2",
          "html": "&radic;3 : 2&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "1 : &radic;3",
          "html": "1 : &radic;3&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Given:-</strong></p>\n\n<p>&ang;OCB = 60&deg;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><strong>Concept Used:</strong></p>\n\n<p>Diagonals of a rhombus are&nbsp;&perp;&nbsp;bisectors to each other</p>\n\n<p>cos&theta; = Adjacent Side/Hypotenuse</p>\n\n<p>cos60&deg; = 1/2&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><strong>Calculation:</strong></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">ABCD is a rhombus,&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">Let sides of a rhombus be a units,</span></p>\n\n<p><img src=\"https:https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/23/01/F1_Vinanti_SSC_02.01.23_D1_V3.png\" /></p>\n\n<p>In the given figure,&nbsp;&Delta; COB,&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>cos &ang;OCB =&nbsp;<span style=\"\">cos60&deg; = 1/2&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr; 1/2 = OC/CB</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr; 1/2 = OC/a</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr; OC = a/2</span></p>\n\n<p>Hence, AC = 2&nbsp;&times; OC = 2&nbsp;&times; a/2 = a</p>\n\n<p>Now in&nbsp;&Delta; AOB,&nbsp;&ang; AOB = 90&deg;&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>Using Pythagoras&nbsp;theorem,&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">AB<sup>2</sup> = OA<sup>2</sup>&nbsp;+ OB<sup>2</sup></span></p>\n\n<p>&rArr; a<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span>&nbsp;= (a/2)<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span>&nbsp;+ OB<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span></p>\n\n<p>&rArr; OB<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span>&nbsp;= a<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span>&nbsp;- (a/2)<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr; OB</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;= 3a<sup>2</sup>/4</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr; OB =&nbsp;&radic;3a/2</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">Hence, BD&nbsp;= 2&nbsp;&times; OB&nbsp;= 2&nbsp;&times; &radic;3a/2 = &radic;3a</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">AC : BD =&nbsp;a:&radic;3</span><span style=\"\">a</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;AC : BD = 1:&radic;3</span></p>\n\n<p><strong><span style=\"\">&there4; The ratio of AC: BD is 1 : &radic;3&nbsp;</span></strong></p>\n",
      "images": [
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/23/01/F1_Vinanti_SSC_02.01.23_D1_V3.png",
        "https:https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/23/01/F1_Vinanti_SSC_02.01.23_D1_V3.png"
      ],
